From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hhh2210 <hzy2210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add LeadSec NC child, Quick Mode and Vendor ID compatibility

Make a native charon interoperate with the LeadSec PowerVPN gateway for
NC (network-connection) resources, matching what the vendor helper puts
on the wire:

- child_cfg/vici: per-child private ADDRULE envelope
  (leadsec_addrule) and Quick Mode proposal number
  (leadsec_proposal_number), loaded over VICI.
- quick_mode: send the ADDRULE payload under HASH(3) and use the
  configured proposal number.
- isakmp_vendor: for initiators whose children carry the ADDRULE
  envelope, send the NC IPv4 vendor ID and, when
  charon.leadsec_new_client_vid = yes, the "NEW CLIENT" vendor ID.
  Without NEW CLIENT the gateway completes IKE and forwards inbound
  traffic, but never returns ESP for the virtual IP (0/6 vs 6/6 A/B,
  then 10/10 consecutive; see docs/evidence/native-strongswan-backend.md).
- kernel_libipsec: never adopt a virtual IP already owned by another
  interface.

